{
  "interpretation": "The patch implements a thread-local SQLite connection pool in app/db.py, replacing per-request connection creation. Validation passed, confirming API contract compliance (0 semantic mismatches, 100% success rate). Performance metrics show significant improvement: mean latency dropped from 1.229ms to 1.030ms (16.2% reduction), and p95 latency decreased from 2.038ms to 1.778ms. The decision cites a 11.7% relative improvement over epsilon. Noise analysis indicates reduced variability (CV 0.086 to 0.031). However, the implementation uses thread-local pools, which may not reuse connections across different worker threads in async/multi-worker environments, potentially limiting gains if the bottleneck is thread-local connection overhead rather than global contention. The plan's hypothesis about eliminating connect/close overhead is supported by the data, but the effectiveness depends on request distribution across threads.",
  "limitations": [
    "Thread-local pooling may not reuse connections across different worker threads, limiting scalability benefits in multi-worker deployments.",
    "Improvement magnitude (11.7%) is modest; further gains may require async I/O or global pooling strategies.",
    "No data on long-term connection stability or memory usage under sustained load.",
    "Epsilon threshold for acceptance is not explicitly defined in the provided metrics."
